reasury and Federal Reserve System\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [828, 1843, 1514, 1946], \"page_id\": 95}], \"content\": \"In accordance with Fund policies the United States has the right to draw foreign currencies equivalent to its reserve position in the Fund virtually automatically if needed. Under appropriate conditions the United States could draw additional amounts equal to the United States quota. See Table IFS-5.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [830, 1943, 1530, 2042], \"page_id\": 95}], \"content\": \"Reserve position includes, and gold stock excludes, $259 million gold subscription to the Fund in June 1965 for a U.S. quota increase which became effective on February 23, 1966. In figures published by the Fund from June 1965 through January 1966, this gold subscription was included in the U.S. gold stock and excluded from the reserve position.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [830, 2042, 1507, 2121], \"page_id\": 95}], \"content\": \"1/ Includes gain of $67 million resulting from revaluation of the German mark in October 1969, of which $13 million represents gain on German mark holdings at time of revaluation. See also footnotes 3 and 4, Table IFS4.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [46, 74, 80, 100], \"page_id\": 96}], \"content\": \"84\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1248, 48, 1563, 103], \"page_id\": 96}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [477, 110, 1113, 139], \"page_id\": 96}], \"content\": \"INTERNATIONAL FINANCIAL STATISTICS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [497, 179, 1107, 213], \"page_id\": 96}], \"content\": \"Table IFS-2. - U.S. Liq