 SECRETARY\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [646, 993, 1073, 1039], \"page_id\": 8}], \"content\": \"The Treasury Bulletin is for sale by the Superintendent of Documents.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [549, 1037, 1192, 1109], \"page_id\": 8}], \"content\": \"U.S. Government Printing Office, Washington, D.C. 20402 Subscription per year $13.50 domestic, $17.00 foreign. Single copy price varies.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1377, 44, 1402, 85], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"I\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [634, 308, 845, 355], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"CONTENTS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [148, 454, 1322, 1785], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"Treasury financing operations. II\\nFederal fiscal operations. 1\\nFederal obligations. 14\\nAccount of the Treasurer of the United States. 18\\nMonetary statistics. 21\\nFederal debt. 22\\nPublic debt operations. 30\\nUnited States savings bonds. 63\\nUnited States savings notes. 67\\nOwnership of Federal securities. 68\\nTreasury survey of ownership 70\\nMarket quotations on Treasury securities. 76\\nAverage yields of long-term bonds. 79\\nNational bank reports. 81\\nInternational financial statistics. 82\\nCapital movements. 87\\nFinancial operations of Government agencies and funds 124\\nCumulative table of contents. 170\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [149, 1846, 1002, 1887], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"Note: Details of figures may not add to totals because of rounding.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [87, 36, 279, 87], \"page_id\": 9}], \"content\": \"June 1970\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [36, 48, 78, 86], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"II\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1275, 22, 1580, 72], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [571, 298, 1072, 336], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"Treasury Financing Operations\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [43, 466, 376, 500], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"9-Month and One-year Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [48, 512, 790, 805], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"On May 20 tenders were invited for $500 million, or thereabouts, of 272-day Treasury bills, representing an additional amount of bills dated February 28, 1970, maturing February 28, 1971, and for $1.2 billion, or thereabouts, of 365-day Treasury bills to be dated May 31, 1970, to mature May 31, 1971, both series to be issued June 1. These issues were to refund $1,501 million of bills maturing May 31. Tenders were opened on May 26.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [50, 819, 788, 968], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"Tenders received for the 272-day bills totaled $1,293 million, of which $500 million was accepted, including $19 million of noncompetitive tenders. The average bank discount rate was 7.353 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [54, 985, 797, 1129], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"Tenders received for the 365-day bills totaled $2,401 million, of which $1,200 million was accepted, including $54 million of noncompetitive tenders. The average bank discount rate was 7.277 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [55, 1150, 371, 1179], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"13-Week and 26-Week Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [55, 1191, 801, 1381], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"Issues of regular weekly Treasury bills in May totaled $12.4 billion, replacing $12.0 billion of maturing bills. There were four 91-day issues of $1.8 billion and three 182-day and one 183-day issues of $1.3 billion. Average rates for the new issues are shown in the following table.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [55, 1487, 810, 2001], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th colspan=\\\"3\\\">13-week (Additional amount of bills of original maturity of 26 weeks)</th><th colspan=\\\"2\\\">26-week</th></tr><tr><th colspan=\\\"2\\\">Date of --</th><th>Approximate equivalent annual average rate 1/</th><th>Date of issue</th><th>Approximate equivalent annual average rate 1/</th></tr><tr><th>Additional issue</th><th>Original issue</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr><tr><td>1970 May 7</td><td>1970 Feb. 5</td><td>7.184</td><td>1970 May 7</td><td>7.493</td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td>13</td><td>6.994</td><td>14</td><td>7.201</td></tr><tr><td>21</td><td>19</td><td>6.827</td><td>21</td><td>6.996</td></tr><tr><td>28</td><td>26</td><td>7.133</td><td>28</td><td>7.356</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [853, 449, 1154, 480], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bills - General\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [847, 492, 1591, 757], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"Treasury bills are sold on a bid basis. The face amount is payable without interest at maturity. They are issued in bearer form only, and in denominations of $1,000, $5,000, $10,000, $50,000, $100,000, $500,000, and $1,000,000 (maturity value) 2/. Tenders are received at Federal Reserve banks and branches. Each tender must be for a multiple of $10,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [853, 776, 1589, 1069], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"Banking institutions generally may submit tenders for account of customers. Tenders may be made without deposit by incorporated banks and trust companies and by responsible and recognized dealers in investment securities. Tenders from others must be accompanied by payment of 2 percent of the face amount of bills applied for, unless the tenders are accompanied by an express guaranty of payment by an incorporated bank or trust company.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1081, 1589, 1237], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"Noncompetitive tenders (without stated price), usually for $200,000 or less from any one bidder, are accepted in full at the average price of accepted competitive bids for an issue.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [861, 1249, 1587, 1467], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"Payment for accepted tenders must be made or complete on the date of issue, in cash or other immediately available funds or in a like face amount of Treasury bills maturing on that date. Payment for 13-week, 26-week, 9-month, and one year bills may not be made by credit in Treasury tax and loan accounts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [865, 1489, 1396, 1520], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"Foreign Series and Foreign Currency Series\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [872, 1528, 1584, 1717], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"Foreign series securities issued in May totaled $2.3 million, consisting of three certificates of indebtedness at two notes. Redemptions for the month totaled $331 million. At the end of May foreign series securities outstanding totaled $2.534 million. (Details are shown on page 59.)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [876, 1734, 1591, 1991], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"Foreign currency series securities issued in May consisted of two notes denominated in Swiss francs equivalent $54 million. Redemptions for the month totaled an equivalent of $53 million. At the end of May foreign currency series securities outstanding totaled an equivalent of $1,366 million and were denominated in German marks and Swiss franc (Details are shown on page 62.)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [64, 2008, 1555, 2138], \"page_id\": 10}], \"content\": \"Note: Details of Treasury market financing operations are shown elsewhere in tables on public debt operations.\\n1/ Bank discount basis.\\n2/ Effective with the Treasury bills issued on March 5, 1970, the $1,000 and $5,000 denominations are no longer authorized on original issue.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [14, 27, 195, 70], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"June 1970\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1495, 34, 1518, 70], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"1\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [541, 85, 998, 109], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"FEDERAL FISCAL OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [488, 141, 1027, 174], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"Table FFO-1. - Summary of Fiscal Operations\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [668, 199, 905, 228], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [14, 225, 1536, 1047], \"page_id\": 11}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th rowspan=\\\"2\\\">Fiscal year or month</th><th colspan=\\\"5\\\">The expenditure account</th><th colspan=\\\"3\\\">Loan account 1/</th><th colspan=\\\"