-2 brings together the various statistical components of the liabilities which enter into the United States balance of payments calculated on the liquidity basis. The inclusion of the United States reserve position in the International Monetary Fund in Table IFS-1 requires that the\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [822, 254, 1550, 337], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"\\\"holdings of dollars\\\" of the Fund be excluded from the data on liabilities to foreigners, in order to avoid double counting.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [826, 349, 1552, 431], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"Table IFS-3 presents an area breakdown of United States liquid liabilities to official institutions of foreign countries.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [828, 448, 1552, 533], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"Table IFS-4 shows United States Treasury nonmarketable bonds and notes issued to official institutions of foreign countries.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [824, 543, 1550, 601], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"Table IFS-5 sets forth the factors which affect the United States position in the International Monetary Fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [824, 620, 1552, 703], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"Table IFS-6 presents United States net monetary gold transactions with foreign countries and international and regional organizations.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [580, 1083, 1033, 1112], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"Table IFS-1. - U.S. Reserve Assets\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [676, 1141, 918, 1180], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\